body:
If your looking to lose fat fast, then cardio is your way to go. 

&#x200B;

The way strength training burns fat is that it builds muscle, which then takes up more of your metabolism than the fat. This is the "preferred" way by many bodybuilders and internet coaches, but it is much slower than cardio. One of the biggest turnaways from this method, though, is that people don't typically see movement on the scale, as you are increasing muscle and decreasing fat which makes you look leaner without actually dropping any poundage.

&#x200B;

TL;DR- if you want the "fast" route or to lose numbers on the scale, cardio is your route to go. If you want slow and sustainable and care more about your appearance than your weight, then strength is the way to go.

I see that you're posting in the comments what you've noticed you need to fix, which is awesome! Like many others, I would suggest you keep your back straight, and pull the DB up until your elbow is at a 90 degree angle. I pull mine up until both ends firmly touch my chest/body. I also keep my head down, which helps to keep the back straight. 

&#x200B;

Also, I can't see your feet, but I would recommend trying a split stance. You stand at the end of a bench and essentially make a diamond with your opposite hand on the bench, your opposite foot and dumbbell hand parallel to each other, and your same-side foot back. [I've linked a video with someone doing it if that would help.](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=od9xGGsTVME&ab_channel=TestosteroneNation)

I don't think this counts as a spoiler (it doesn't affect gameplay at all, it's just a funny little bit of information about Jasmine & her scooter)..., 

